# Local Workspace File — Do Not Modify

`*.local.code-workspace` files (e.g. `TNC-Hydrology-Water-Flow.local.code-workspace`) are **intentionally authored** machine-local VS Code / Cursor workspace files. They hold project-specific settings that are **not cosmetic throwaway content**.

## ✅ DO

- Leave the file exactly as-is when its contents are not directly relevant to the requested task.
- If changes are required, preserve **all existing keys** under `"settings"`, including `workbench.colorCustomizations` and its title bar color values.

## ❌ DO NOT

- Remove, strip, or omit `workbench.colorCustomizations` or any of its sub-keys (`titleBar.activeBackground`, `titleBar.activeForeground`, `titleBar.inactiveBackground`, `titleBar.inactiveForeground`, `titleBar.border`).
- Treat appearance settings in this file as non-essential or clutter. They are **deliberate workspace identity markers** that distinguish this project's window from others.
- "Clean up" or "simplify" this file without explicit developer instruction.

## Why these settings exist

The title bar colors serve as a **visual workspace identifier** — a deliberate design choice so this project window is immediately recognizable when multiple Cursor windows are open side-by-side.
